A||||17||Julian||Tech question on GT vs. Formula||||5||
Z||000000||Julian||11-19-2000||03:04 PM||||I have an 88 Fiero Mera (rebody) that was built in 1988 on a Fiero Formula. I know that in 1997 they built the Mera on GT's.  Since the entire car is a rebody what differences are there from a GT to a Formula? Are they cosmetic? Like interior trim, steering wheel? Or does it go deeper like suspension? Horsepower? <P>I'm new at this so talk slow....LOL<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/meralogo.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||11-19-2000||04:04 PM||||GT's and Formuli are the same except for cosmetic differences. Usually Formulas didn't have as many options. Pwr windows etc.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ed||11-19-2000||08:08 PM||||But there are differences in the chassis of '84's to '87's, and '88's.  Brakes, suspension, wheel offset.  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tom88gt||11-19-2000||08:16 PM||||Formula is only an 88.  The 88 GT and Formula are mechanically identical.  GT has all the extras PW, PL, power mirrors, elec trunk release, rear defroster, etc as standard equipment.  You can get all the same on the Formula but it's extra.  With all the same options, the Formula is cheaper, and faster (the GT body is heavier) so that is why the 88 Mera uses a Formula and not a GT.  87 and prior there was no Formula option so a GT was the only donor platform to use.<P>But no, you are not lossing or missing any power or handling because your Mera is a Formula.  If you don't have power mirrors, trunk, defrost you can add real easy.<P>I'm adding those to my Formula amd then will try to find GT body panels (don't mind the extra weight cause I prefer the GT looks).  Thus my name (looking towards the future).||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phil||11-19-2000||09:13 PM||||Anybody know the actual weight diff between the Formula and GT  both with the same options?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Will||11-19-2000||09:17 PM||||The body panel weight difference betwen GT and Formula might amount to 15 lbs. Not enough to matter.<BR>What little weight difference there was came from the power options on the GT.<BR>With the marginal weight difference, you will be hard pressed to find a consistent difference in performance between the two. Driver skill will be a much bigger factor than the differences in the cars.||||reg||1
Z||000006||WKDFIRO||11-20-2000||06:42 AM||||I looked this very query up in the "Fiero" book by Witzenberg...<P>1988 GT curb weight: 2735 lbs.<BR>1988 Formula curbweight:? (Doesn't have it!)<P>But! If we look back a year and compare the 87 SE: 2567<BR>87 GT: 2708<BR>Both with V6 but one it the notchback. <P>And just for fun:<BR>87 Coupe: 2546<BR>84 Coupe: 2464 (precooked) <P>Just kidding 84 owners!<BR>||||reg||12
Z||000007||ThatRickGuy||11-20-2000||08:58 AM||||The formula did not have pwr mirrors, sub woofer, or fastback, they weren't even options. Other then that, their identical. as fro the 88 formula curb weight, my auto w/ T-tops, power windows, locks and cruise weighs in right arround 2600 I beleive.<p>[This message has been edited by ThatRickGuy (edited 11-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||fiero56||11-20-2000||10:45 AM||||There were 94 Formulas from the factory with pm, 8 with subwoofer, 279 with remote deck release.||||reg||1
