Z||000015||fiero56||11-21-2000||05:26 PM||||Spotters guide is the best thing you can possible buy.<P>Mark Corbin is the man behind this little 80 page books. They are $4 + $1 shipping. Send check or money order to:<P>Fiero Spotters Guide<BR>5474 S.R. 19<BR>Galion, OH 44833<P>Really is a great deal. All info inside is proven by actual documentation, there are no guesses in it.<BR>Nothing about the Mera in it, but there were 730 Fieros exported to Canada in '88.<P>ThatRickGuy: you were correct that they weren't options. I don't know the story behind the Formula numbers I posted, I'm sure Mark could supply the info about them. <p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 11-21-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000016||88formula||11-21-2000||09:14 PM||||According to the Brooklands fiero book the weight difference is 50lbs.<P>That makes a difference of about 1/10 of a second to 60 mph and 1/10 of a second in the quarter mile and 1-mph.<BR>||||reg||1
